# Adaptive agent policy (Ingenium)

Product locks in `AGENTS.md` and `MEMORY.md` win over this file. This file only governs how work is routed and verified.

- Ask what minimum capability the next step needs. Do not map "architecture" or "UI" to a brand.
- Score escalation pressure only when the route is unclear: complexity, uncertainty, failure consequence, constraint density, verification difficulty, irreversibility (0–3 each) plus prior failed attempts (0–2). Bands: 0–5 cheap or a tool; 6–9 strong generalist; 10–13 higher effort; 14–16 frontier; 17–20 frontier plus an independent "what could be wrong?" review.
- Escalate only a diagnosed model-capability gap, and only the unresolved slice.
- Deterministic work uses tests, linters, RPC probes, and SQL. Do not spend a model call to compute what a tool can check.
- UI work loads the installed Prime skills for that surface (taste, motion, copy, accessibility) before editing screens. Motion is tasteful, interruptible, transform/opacity, under 300ms, and reduced-motion safe. Operate-mode screens stay dense and calm.
- Stop when the gate for the current slice is met. Do not polish past the written done condition.
- Long-running phase state lives in `docs/plans/INGENIUM_NEXT_PHASE_PROGRESS.md`.
